// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// use this to manage Sarah's commentary and make it work across scenarios
// TOC: There are no TOC entries and this is ordered|nokeep:  this means the next page will be read each time it is opened
// The default page text entries for goal == goalClosePortal
// Note that the "visible" directives may change during the game, so pages with visibility rules might show out of order

Language English

BOOK SarahPatter Ordered No Keep

    Page Dvm
        Page Is Visible When foundDvm

        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The {c:QItemDVM} is
            a spell book. It contains many powerful spells, including how to
            open and close portals, and how to interrupt a ritual that has been
            started.
            
            <<If you cannot stop {c:CustomMonsterDavidSmythe} in time,
            you may need to perform a closing ritual. Closing portals is easier
            than opening them but it takes time. With the portal open, many
            horrors could come through while you are trying to close it. You
            must be prepared. Read the book carefully and read it soon.>>
        """

        If goal == goalFeedPortal Or goal == goalClosePortal Then Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The {c:QItemDVM} is
            a spell book. It contains many powerful spells, including how to
            open and close portals. You should read it to better understand
            what is happening.>>
        """
    End Page Dvm

    Page Candles
        Page Is Visible When foundCandles

        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<There's a part of
            the house that is too dark to enter without light. The candles you
            found should help. If we move fast enough, maybe we can stop
            {c:CustomMonsterDavidSmythe} from opening the portal.>>
        """
    End Page Candles

    Page ElderSign
        Page Is Visible When foundElderSign

        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The
            {c:QItemElderSign} is a powerful protective symbol. It can be used
            to ward off evil creatures and protect people from harm. If you
            have it, you should keep it with you at all times.>>
        """

        If goal == goalClosePortal Then Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The
            {c:QItemElderSign} is an important part of the closing ritual. It
            seals the portal permanently. When the closing ritual was
            performed 10 years ago, our Uncle Henry was able to close the
            portal, but he died before he could seal it.>>
        """

        If goal == goalOpenPortal Then Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The
            {c:QItemElderSign} is important for their plans tonight. It is used
            to either secure or seal a portal. It is good we found it before
            they did.>>
        """

    End Page ElderSign

    Page RitualComponents
        Page Is Visible When foundRitualComponents
		
        Text """
            Sarah reaches out as if to touch the {c:QItemRitualComponents}. <<I
            recognize some of these items from the portal ritual. Both my father
            and the men who tried to stop him brought similar items to help with
            the spells.>>
        """
    End Page RitualComponents

    Page Dagger
        Page Is Visible When foundDagger

        Text """
            Sarah reaches toward the {c:QItemRitualDagger}. <<I recognize this
            dagger,>> she starts. <<It looks like the one my father used in the
            portal ritual. With luck, they need this one and we have it.>>
        """
    End Page Dagger

    Page Journal
        Page Is Visible When foundJournal
        
        Text """
            Sarah looks down and sees you holding the {c:QItemJournal}. <<The
            {c:QItemJournal}! The man who let you in was writing in it all
            week. You should read it carefully.>>
        """
    End Page Journal

    Page Color1
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<You don't remember
            me or what happened 10 years ago. I am your little sister.
            
            <<I will tell you everything you need to know, but first I must
            tell you that David will open a portal
            tonight and you must stop him; if you cannot stop him, you will
            need to close that portal.>>
        """
    End Page Color1

    Page Color2
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The people in this
            town worship a darker god than most. They want to bring their god
            to Earth. 10 years ago, my father cast a ritual to summon It. He
            opened a portal. The power it possessed was breathtaking and I
            could do nothing to stop it. Somehow, Father summoned local
            townsfolk through the portal to protect his casting, even after he
            was dead. As the portal, I could feel people and monsters
            approaching and passing through me from the other side.>>
        """
    End Page Color2

    Page Color3
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<I could feel the
            ancient one approach from the other side. Suddenly, a group of men
            broke into the altar chamber and began fighting the locals. One man
            went to the altar, killed our father, laid out some materials, and
            spoke words I didn't understand. He closed the portal while his
            friends protected him from what came through it.>>
        """
    End Page Color3

    Page Color4
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator},
            <<Our father believed that personal sacrifice was the most powerful
            magic. The portal is created by binding power to the body of a
            loved one. Father used me to summon the portal. When the portal
            closed, I died with it. The pain of the ritual so engulfed me that
            I can still feel it.>>
        """
    End Page Color4
    
    Page Color5
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<You found out what
            was going to happen a week before the ritual. Members of Father's
            church did something to you. After that, you followed orders
            without question. You helped Father bind me during the ritual. From
            what they said at the time, you probably cannot remember anything
            about the ritual or anything before. It's why you don't know who
            you are or remember what happened that night.>>
        """
    End Page Color5

    Page Color6
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, <<The day of the
            ritual, two of my friends came to visit me. When Father told them I
            wasn't allowed out, they sneaked to my window and crawled in when I
            opened it. Father was furious. I'm not sure who strangled them or
            who dragged them to the yard. I was burning alive when the portal
            closed, then my body was dumped with my friends. It wasn't until
            then that I knew they were dead. I smoldered for several days,
            alive and conscious until the end.>>
        """
    End Page Color6
    
    Page Color7
        Text """
            Sarah whispers to {c:EventChosenInvestigator}, “I don't know who
            the other men were, but the one who closed the portal was our uncle
            Henry--Father's brother. I think there's something special about
            our family; there are things only we can do. It's why Father could
            summon the portal, and why Uncle Henry could close it.
            
            <<You probably share the family abilities. You must trust yourself
            to know what to do.>>
        """
    End Page Color7
End Book SarahPatter

